    ipbes:SubChapter <http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/sch/LDR18-7.2> ;
    ipbes:hasDescription """Hatching indicates regions where the multi-model mean is small compared to natural internal variability (i.e., less than one standard deviation of natural internal variability in 20-year means). Stippling indicates regions where the multi-model mean is large compared to natural internal variability (i.e., greater than two standard deviations of natural internal variability in 20-year means) and where at least 90% of models agree on the sign of change. Source: IPCC (2014b).

RCP2.6 RCP8.5""" ;
    dcterms:identifier "Figure7.12" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Maps of the CMIP5 multi-model mean results for the scenarios RCP2.6 and RCP8.5 in 2081-2100 of average percent change in annual mean precipitation." .

