    ipbes:Report ipbes:LDR18 ;
    ipbes:hasDescription "Food security is a multi-dimensional phenomenon and is a critical factor in achieving human well-being and quality of life. Historically, it has had several research definitions and policy usages (FAO, 2003). For this report, we adopt the definition drafted by FAO (2002) in the State of Food Insecurity: “food security [is] a situation that exists when all people, at all times, have physical, social and economic access to sufficient, safe and nutritious food that meets their dietary needs and food preferences for an active and healthy life. ”" ;
    dcterms:identifier "5.3" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Food security" .

